# Copy to `.env` and fill in, then restart the dev server.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Which of these you need depends on WHICH CHILD this rapper mounts. Nothing
# here is required by rapper itself.

# ── VITE_TILES_HOST — needed by: getCache_OfflineMap ────────────────────────
# WHY THIS EXISTS: getCache_OfflineMap ships with no tile-server origin baked
# in, so that installing it cannot bill someone else's Cloudflare account. The
# child reads VITE_TILES_HOST at boot and configures itself from it.
#
# ⛔ IF IT IS UNSET, THE OFFLINE MAP DOWNLOADS NOTHING AND SAYS ALMOST NOTHING.
# No /pack request is sent at all — packUrl() returns null and the download is
# skipped before the network. The satellite still appears (different service),
# so it looks like "roads are broken" rather than "no tile host configured".
# The only clue is one console.warn line at startup. (It was console.info until
# 27 Aug 2026, and a default DevTools level filter hid it entirely — which is
# why 204 KB × 39 areas of real work could run and print nothing visible.)
#
# Point it at your OWN offline-tiles Worker:
VITE_TILES_HOST=https://<your-tiles-worker>
#
# Ground Truth's own hosts are tiles-prod.getcache.org and tiles-dev.getcache.org
# — deliberately NOT the default here, because a baked-in production host is a
# bill, not a default (see the child's lib/r2Worker/tilesHost.ts, and the test
# in tierNaming.test.ts that asserts the child bakes in none).
#
# To develop with no Cloudflare account at all, run the local tier — see
# ReTreever/workers/offline-tiles/setupLocalTiles.sh — and use:
#   VITE_TILES_HOST=http://tiles-local.getcache.org:8787

# ── VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN — needed by: getCache_OnlineMap, ReTreever_where ──────
# The online map boots Mapbox GL with this, and ReTreever_where also uses it for
# place-name geocoding.
#
# ⛔ IF IT IS UNSET, NO MAP IS CREATED. Both children now say so on the page and
# name this variable; before 28 Aug 2026 the online map logged only "Mapbox
# access token is required" — naming nothing you could search for — and the
# geocoder interpolated `undefined` into its URL and reported a 401 as
# "Search failed — try again".
#
# Free tokens: https://account.mapbox.com/access-tokens/
VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=
